 "decision": "held: not promoted, exam not opened",
 "rule_outcome": "kept",
 "why_held": "R7f passes the rule (sim +0.236, dev composite +0.385), but its blind-mode outputs equal its visible ones (blind wind R2 0.990 vs visible 0.994 on val_v3; crown 0.707 vs 0.706): the sim wind label tracks the gridMET wind input (r = 0.993), and BI (burning index, computed from wind), ERC and temperature stay in the blind input. With the flag at z = 1000 the network could not use that path; at z = 1 it does. Setting BI to its training mean in blind mode drops the blind-wind correlation with the truth from 0.995 to 0.224. The gain is a wind leak through BI, not a better blind estimate, so the rung does not answer the audit question. Owner decision needed (e.g. also blank BI, and possibly ERC, in blind mode, then repeat the matched pair).",
